1
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone short on money, come to me.

2
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:28,980
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

4
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,640
Thank you for watching.

5
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:43,660
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

6
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,900
Hmm!

7
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,140
Chirp!

8
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,600
Cheh! Cheap ticket!

9
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,260
Gacchyoon!

10
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:57,622
It's just a mirror.

11
00:01:57,672 --> 00:02:00,580
That startled me.
Guess I'll sleep a bit longer.

12
00:02:01,520 --> 00:02:06,160
That's impossible!
Who are you?! No, who are YOU?!

13
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,780
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu too!

14
00:02:09,780 --> 00:02:11,480
W-what's going on?

15
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:13,500
My birthday is

16
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,000
March 3rd.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,960
The dinner I had the day before yesterday

18
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:19,440
was natto fried rice with soup.

19
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,660
What did I get scolded for yesterday?

20
00:02:21,660 --> 00:02:23,880
Skipping work and hanging
out at a manga café,

21
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:24,860
I was napping, so...

22
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:27,080
You! How do you know all that?

23
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,480
How do you know it so well?!

24
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,680
Are you me?

25
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:32,180
Am I you?

26
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:35,000
Are you Ryotsu?

27
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:46,300
Well, it can't be helped
now that it's happened.

28
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:50,360
Since there are two of us now,
let's try to think positively.

29
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:53,220
That's just like me, saying something smart.

30
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,460
So, what exactly do we do?

31
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:57,540
Well, for example,

32
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,660
we could take turns working.

33
00:03:00,660 --> 00:03:05,140
Then we can take turns resting
and get tons more days off!

34
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:08,060
In that case, I'll take today off.

35
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,940
I'm the one who suggested it, you know.

36
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,780
Why don't you show a little restraint?

37
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,760
Why don't you save your fun for later too?

38
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:19,880
No, no, you're the one who should.

39
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,900
Says you, you're the one who should!

40
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,500
You lazy bastard!

41
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,720
Have some shame, you!

42
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:30,520
What?

43
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:32,400
Don't you dare say that to me!

44
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:34,200
Getting cocky for someone who's just me

45
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,500
What's that supposed to mean?

46
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,760
You idiot!

47
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:44,140
Do you know what time it is?

48
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:47,660
How old are you now,
and you still haven't changed that attitude?

49
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,960
Isn't that the wrong
issue to focus on, Chief?

50
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,400
There are two of me now, you know.

51
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:56,460
Stop yelling, you noisy stereo!

52
00:03:57,080 --> 00:04:00,420
At this point,
I won't be surprised by anything you do.

53
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:03,620
Of course, Chief, you're not even
surprised by this much, are you?

54
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,240
They look exactly the same, don't they.

55
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,100
I've always thought he was a strange man,

56
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,000
but I never imagined he
could do something like this.

57
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,520
This is no time to be impressed!

58
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,420
But that's pretty impressive, isn't it?

59
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:19,020
If there are two of you,
you could take turns resting.

60
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:20,940
Coming to work together like this...

61
00:04:20,940 --> 00:04:25,040
No, I thought that at first too,

62
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,500
but thanks to this idiot,

63
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:28,980
what did you just say?

64
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:31,400
Did you just call me an idiot, you bastard?

65
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:36,920
Now that there are two of us,
our workforce has doubled.

66
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:39,900
We'll make up for all the slacking
we've done by working twice as hard.

67
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:40,860
Well then, in that case,

68
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,040
Then, right away, Ryo-chan,

69
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:44,640
What?

70
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:50,620
Every time I call you Ryo-chan,
you both respond, and it gets so confusing.

71
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:53,840
True, both of you look
exactly like our senior officer.

72
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:54,720
Alright.

73
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:58,160
Then let's do it this way.

74
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:01,040
There, done.

75
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:03,480
Let's say I'm Ryotsu A.

76
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:06,340
And you're Ryotsu B.

77
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:08,920
Wait, why am I B?

78
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:11,440
Because you're the second me, obviously.

79
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,400
So I'm A and you're B.

80
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,580
No, that's wrong.

81
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,880
What proof is there that you're
the first one and I'm the second?

82
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:20,440
There's no proof anywhere, is there?

83
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,800
R-really?

84
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:25,600
Somehow, by the way things went,
I'm the original Ryotsu, and

85
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:28,500
I thought you were the copy or the fake,

86
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:32,300
but from your point of view,
I can only look like the copy or the fake.

87
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,020
Right, after all, I'm also me.

88
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:37,380
Fine, let's settle it
with rock-paper-scissors.

89
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:40,640
Alright, here we go. Rock first!

90
00:05:42,740 --> 00:05:44,400
I said rock first, didn't I?

91
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,400
You too? Fine, no "rock first" this time.

92
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,880
Straight to the showdown.

93
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:50,480
Rock, paper, scissors!

94
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,160
Ugh, no going after me!

95
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,640
You human scum!

96
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:01,400
If you two can't decide on your own,
I'll decide for you.

97
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:04,300
You're A, and you're B.

98
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:07,000
Now that's settled, get to work already.

99
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,520
Yes.

100
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:18,140
Why do I have to work on a mikan crate?

101
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,600
Senpai, do you have a sec?

102
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:21,660
What is it?

103
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,900
I only need one of you, though.

104
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:28,480
Then B, you go help him.

105
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,660
Do it yourself! Drop dead!

106
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:33,100
Ryo-chan, can you come help for a sec?

107
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,280
Hey B, she's calling you.

108
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,280
It's you she called, A.

109
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:39,680
But Reiko said "Ryo-chan."

110
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,100
You're Ryo-chan, aren't you?

111
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,420
So are you.

112
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:45,640
Anyway, I don't accept being Ryotsu B.

113
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:48,400
The Chief decided it,
so there's nothing we can do.

114
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:50,680
Why do I have to work on a mikan crate?

115
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,540
Because you're B.

116
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:55,100
If you don't like being B,
you can be Ryotsu No. 2.

117
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,180
If you two just split the work,
it'd be done, wouldn't it?

118
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,640
At the very least,
you two should do one person's work.

119
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,300
You good-for-nothing.

120
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:05,860
Good-for-nothing.

121
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,380
What's wrong?

122
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:15,460
Nothing.

123
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,000
What's wrong with you?

124
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,700
M-me? I'm just,

125
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,120
going to the bathroom.

126
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:21,760
What a coincidence.

127
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,140
I'm going to the bathroom too.

128
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,780
The bathroom isn't that way, you idiot!

129
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:32,120
I've seen through your
behavior patterns long ago.

130
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,300
I knew you'd be wanting
to slack off about now.

131
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:39,280
Damn it,
it's your fault for getting up so obviously!

132
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:41,700
You're the one lying so obviously!

133
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,600
What did you say? You're just B!

134
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,440
What?

135
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,820
Stop it!

136
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:46,980
Yes.

137
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:50,040
It's patrol time.

138
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,600
Chief, I'm not slacking off this time.

139
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:55,540
Today's my turn, after all.

140
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,320
Right, right.

141
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,100
We don't both need to go.

142
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:00,940
One of you stay behind
and sort the paperwork.

143
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:04,400
Fine, let's settle this one way.

144
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,660
Just settle it fair and square.

145
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,140
Forget it, I'll decide.

146
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:11,020
Ryotsu, you stay behind.

147
00:08:11,020 --> 00:08:13,560
Ryotsu, go on patrol properly.

148
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,420
Yes, I'm heading out.

149
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,970
Being alone is nice.

150
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:25,400
Serves you right, Ryotsu.

151
00:08:28,940 --> 00:08:30,500
How about it, Mr. Ryotsu?

152
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,380
It's just Honda.

153
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:36,300
What's going on?
You look like you're having a great time.

154
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:37,540
Well, yeah.

155
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:39,340
That's right.

156
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,560
Alright.

157
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,960
Damn it, why is it always me?

158
00:08:48,580 --> 00:08:50,260
There you are, senpai!

159
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:50,900
What?

160
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:54,720
What do you mean,
"what"? Pay back the money from earlier.

161
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:58,020
What money are you talking about?

162
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:04,120
What are you talking about? You said earlier that you'd pay me
back right away and to come get it from the police box later.

163
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:10,180
I don't know anything. I never borrowed money from you.
Besides, today is the first time I've ever met you.

164
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:13,740
Don't play dumb.

165
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:15,500
Come on, pay me back quickly.

166
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,760
I have to pay for the motorcycle parts,
you know.

167
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:20,220
I don't know.

168
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,040
This is Kankichi Ryotsu

169
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:29,960
Look, I've really had it with you today.

170
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,140
Did I do something?

171
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:34,920
Don't mess around! On our patrol car!

172
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,060
After you went and did this!

173
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:40,100
I don't know anything. I didn't do a thing.

174
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:45,120
What are you talking about?
We saw you scribbling on it right there.

175
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:50,460
Maybe B did it.
This must be the work of my other self!

176
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:53,260
What nonsense are you babbling about?

177
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,580
Hurry up and wipe off this graffiti.

178
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,680
Please give me back my money too.

179
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,880
A pig is flying in the sky.

180
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:04,720
No! Ah! Look!

181
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,580
Wait!

182
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:07,720
Senpai!

183
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:10,833
Damn it! That B guy!

184
00:10:10,883 --> 00:10:15,700
Blaming it on me and
doing whatever he pleases!

185
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:21,080
Wait a second. I see, I should do it too.

186
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:22,560
Hehehe.

187
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,078
Hehehe. That A guy,

188
00:10:27,128 --> 00:10:29,800
he must be in big trouble right about now.

189
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:30,900
Serves him right.

190
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:31,800
We'll see about that.

191
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,340
You've been doing whatever you pleased,
haven't you?

192
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,540
You'd better be prepared for this.

193
00:10:38,540 --> 00:10:39,920
What are you talking about?

194
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:41,600
Hmph, don't play dumb with me.

195
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,380
But this is where it ends.

196
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:44,660
Look at that.

197
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:49,560
How dare you do that to my Sanbara-yan's...

198
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:52,520
What did you do to our doggie?

199
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,960
That's my Bon, how dare you!

200
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,420
Give back our kid's snack!

201
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,440
W-what is that?

202
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,480
Just like you did to me.

203
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:07,800
Blaming me and doing all kinds of things, what?
You'd better run around and reflect on your life while you still can

204
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,200
Do you remember?

205
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,660
Shut up!

206
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:20,840
Hey, don't you move from there! Ugh, everyone,
that territory over there is supposed to be...

207
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:23,760
Damn, this side is territory too!

208
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:25,940
Aaaaaah!

209
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:27,580
Noooo!

210
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,540
Noooo!

211
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:30,120
Noooo!

212
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:30,840
Noooo!

213
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:34,440
You idiot.

214
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,440
It's all your fault to begin with.

215
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,080
That's what you get for
calling me B or number two.

216
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,740
What did you say, you fake!

217
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:43,000
What? You want a fight?

218
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,660
Nooo -

219
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:46,760
Hey, Ryo-chan!

220
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,240
No way -

221
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,300
Ahh -

222
00:11:55,520 --> 00:12:12,160
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go, go...

223
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,485
This has to be a nightmare.

224
00:12:14,535 --> 00:12:17,080
Tomorrow,
everything will surely be back to normal.

225
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:35,525
Could it be... no way,

226
00:12:35,575 --> 00:12:38,820
What on earth is going on here?

227
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:54,160
Well, I don't know how this happened, but

228
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,820
anyway, there are six of us now.

229
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:58,900
What do we do now?

230
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,220
Well, in this case,

231
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:06,200
if we take turns resting,
that's six days off a week!

232
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:07,860
Banzai!

233
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,160
Yeah, as expected of me,
I really understand things!

234
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:17,940
So, I'll do my best today.
Alright then, I'll take today off.

235
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:20,040
Sounds good, then.

236
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:29,640
Idiots! What is this mess? This is what happens when you
don't lead a proper life as police officers day to day!

237
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:34,000
Do you understand? Do you understand?
Don't ask me that, sheesh...

238
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,740
Don't talk back!

239
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:45,100
But yesterday there were two of you,
and today there are six?

240
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:46,940
As usual, it's a complete mess.

241
00:13:46,940 --> 00:13:49,420
I wonder how many there'll be tomorrow.

242
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:50,800
Don't scare me, Reiko.

243
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,840
This room's already cramped enough.

244
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,400
If it gets any bigger,
we won't even have room to sleep.

245
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:57,720
They'll even stick the meal bills on me.

246
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:00,140
Even the cops had a rough time of it,
you know!

247
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:03,920
Welcome!

248
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:05,840
First things first, food.

249
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,540
Nothing gets done on an empty stomach,
after all.

250
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:19,320
That'll be 17,502 yen.

251
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:20,020
What?

252
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:22,040
You guys are buying way too much.

253
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,040
You're one to talk.

254
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,480
What about you, then?

255
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:26,820
Don't buy that disgusting
manga first thing in the morning.

256
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:29,220
You're buying the same manga too,
aren't you?

257
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,660
Hold on a second.

258
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,880
I just realized something.

259
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,400
There are six of us now, but...

260
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:37,260
Do we each have six wallets?

261
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,560
Still only one wallet

262
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:50,260
So there's only one after all?

263
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:51,680
What else can we do?

264
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,680
Enough to pay for food for six of us,

265
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,820
I'm not rich.

266
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:56,360
True enough.

267
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,860
But how do we split it?

268
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:58,780
Yeah.

269
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,500
There's a pork cutlet flying!

270
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Damn it, if that's how it is,
first come, first served!

271
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:10,140
Hey, you bastard! The croquette is mine!

272
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:12,840
I'll take the rice! And the sausage!

273
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,380
I won't hand the pickles over to anyone!

274
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:16,749
Phew,

275
00:15:16,799 --> 00:15:20,497
thanks to that, all of us are in this state.

276
00:15:20,547 --> 00:15:23,040
This is going to be tough from now on,
isn't it?

277
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:26,800
But now that there are six of you, work should go faster.
That's a good thing, isn't it?

278
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:31,100
Yeah, I see.
That's why you need to work hard.

279
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,600
Work hard, work hard.

280
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:39,700
Work hard, work hard.

281
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:47,140
Yeah, forget a full-fledged criminal,
now we're only a sixth of one.

282
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:56,660
They really are hopeless. But at this rate, we can't tell them apart.
Yeah, even two was confusing, and now that it's six, it's even more...

283
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:59,340
completely impossible to tell.
Then how about...

284
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,020
Hey.

285
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:09,820
Didn't this start a fight yesterday?
Enough complaining, just get to work.

286
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:10,580
Yes.

287
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:19,100
Well, it's happened, so there's nothing for it.
For now, let's all do our best under one roof, six of us.

288
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:22,500
Right, everyone, let's head out!

289
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:25,880
I'm off!

290
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,560
Be safe out there.

291
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:32,060
Patrolling with lots of energy again today.

292
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,560
Hey, Egu, stop getting in the way!

293
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,140
Yes! I've got the lead!

294
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:38,980
What's this? I like it.

295
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:40,380
Hey, quit getting in the way!

296
00:16:40,940 --> 00:16:42,400
Hey, move it forward again!

297
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,680
Ugh, I've hit my limit.

298
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:45,160
Then I'm taking it.

299
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:49,120
Two cheeses.

300
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,320
Let's eat!

301
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:12,880
So tired.

302
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:18,960
That bastard Chief went out of
his way to dump so much work on us.

303
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:19,520
And seriously,

304
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,280
Today, thanks to the kindness of the bakery,

305
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,920
