pile of bread crusts.

306
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:28,940
A real feast after so long!

307
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:30,960
Itadakimasu.

308
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,200
Let's see, let's see.

309
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,280
What's the matter? Aren't you eating?

310
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:44,440
I... I've really had enough of

311
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,420
this. I've reached my limit!

312
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,200
What's wrong, D?

313
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:55,540
I was supposed to be living
a carefree life on my own.

314
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:58,100
And yet five more roommates have shown up.

315
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,760
I can't even get a proper meal.

316
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:00,820
There's nowhere to sleep.

317
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:01,980
I've had enough.

318
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,980
I'm leaving this house.

319
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:04,900
Hey, D.

320
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:14,440
Maybe you're right, D.

321
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,300
We've just been living as six somehow,

322
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:22,320
and it's definitely not normal.
This isn't the life I wanted.

323
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:23,680
Hey, you in?

324
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:27,140
I'm leaving too.
Thanks for everything until now.

325
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,140
Hey, you guys too.

326
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,640
If we keep living together like this,
trouble will surely happen again.

327
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,640
When that happens, there's no
point in Ryotsus fighting each other.

328
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:47,500
So we're leaving too. See you.

329
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:49,540
Wait a minute!

330
00:18:57,780 --> 00:19:00,180
The other senior ones are at home!?

331
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:03,540
Such selfish guys.

332
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,860
Really, just like Ryo-chan.

333
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,920
But where do they all end up sleeping?

334
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,260
How would I know?

335
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:15,100
Well, I've been thinking it's annoying too.

336
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:17,860
I can eat alone, and the room is spacious.

337
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:19,240
Nothing to complain about.

338
00:19:26,420 --> 00:19:28,240
And now, the weather forecast.

339
00:19:28,860 --> 00:19:30,900
With a strong cold front
coming from the continent,

340
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:33,180
the Japanese archipelago
is experiencing a typical

341
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:35,920
winter pressure pattern, with high pressure
to the west and low pressure to the east.

342
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:38,920
Tonight will be especially bitterly cold.

343
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:41,340
Next, the weather in each region.

344
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,260
What? You came back after all?

345
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,140
Honestly, you do whatever the hell you want.

346
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:51,180
So you finally came back

347
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:55,220
Sorry, the neighbor's not home,
so I'll leave the package

348
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:56,080
Ah...

349
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:57,280
Thanks for your business.

350
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:06,700
Hey, we can't squeeze in again.

351
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:07,980
Then I'm taking it.

352
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:16,260
Damn it!

353
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:19,280
You guys are a real handful.

354
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,800
If we had a day off,

355
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,640
I'd head to the pachinko parlor first.

356
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:31,060
Damn it!

357
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:32,240
I'm flat broke.

358
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,980
What am I supposed to do now?

359
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:35,880
Yeah.

360
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,960
Looks like you got wiped out.

361
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,339
Here he comes. Did you come to laugh at me?

362
00:20:43,389 --> 00:20:45,560
Come back.
Sounds like it's going to be cold tonight.

363
00:20:46,300 --> 00:20:47,360
But I...

364
00:20:48,060 --> 00:20:50,960
What are you talking about?
That room is our room, right?

365
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:52,440
Yeah.

366
00:20:59,740 --> 00:21:00,480
Damn it!

367
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:05,120
Dammit, you stupid old man!
I'm never coming back to this house!

368
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:06,420
Ugh...

369
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:07,620
Ugh!

370
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:10,400
Where are you going?

371
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,860
If you sleep outdoors, you'll catch a cold.

372
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:14,540
Come back, you hear?

373
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:16,720
Mind your own business.

374
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:18,280
I've walked out of that room.

375
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,880
How could I go back now?

376
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:20,580
Let's go home.

377
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:24,800
That hurt, didn't it?

378
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,440
You're hurting too, aren't you?

379
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:28,100
I hit you, and it hurts me too.

380
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:31,460
I'm a Ryotsu, but so are you.

381
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,240
That room belongs to Ryotsu.

382
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:35,160
In other words, it's all of our room.

383
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:37,940
Don't be stubborn about
going back to your own room.

384
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:39,700
Come back, will you?

385
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:40,180
D

386
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:41,540
D

387
